  "summary": "54 centroided exposures in 3 visit(s) spanning 262 d. Measured \u03bc\u03b1* = -2404 \u00b1 601, \u03bc\u03b4 = 12183 \u00b1 597 mas/yr vs Gaia DR3 -802, 10362 mas/yr (parallax fixed to 547 mas). Difference -1603, +1821 mas/yr; residual rms 1.79\" (0.29 px). Each visit's median position agrees with the Gaia-predicted position (proper motion + parallax) to within 1.2\u2033 (0.2 px), while the star moved ~7.4\u2033 between first and last visit. Short-wavelength detectors (D1-D3, few points, saturated core) show offsets up to 3.5\u2033. Including a per-visit systematic floor of 0.67\u2033 per axis (\u00b11673 mas/yr on proper motion), the differences are -0.9\u03c3 and +1.0\u03c3; the total motion is detected at 7\u03c3. The floor is estimated from offsets relative to the Gaia prediction, so this consistency check is not independent; the robust results are the detected motion and the \u22641.2\u2033 per-visit agreement. Diagnostic chosen after seeing these offsets (not pre-specified): D5+D6 only gives -2777 \u00b1 467, 11145 \u00b1 463 mas/yr.",
